le="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="e39fee6e-8e53-4e8b-a1ba-4a4eea47617f" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="b82bc3d1-8f6e-4334-b28a-1e6cc3a08cf3"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="f6a85243-ca44-430f-ba63-1a824e853373"><p data-ref="3fc0879a-40e5-40b4-b892-1646b8d4a3e1" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to construct a B-Tree of a given minimum degree. First, insert a list of keys into the B-Tree and print the inorder traversal after all insertions. Then, delete a given set of keys from the B-Tree and again print the inorder traversal. Finally, search for a specific key in the current B-Tree and print whether it is found or not.</p><p data-ref="75bc8ace-d5f2-4b7d-9e35-3f800a3c7890" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="89a47574-8fdb-46de-85d5-60ba6737d309"></p><p data-ref="6212e9d4-3d41-4207-8b4a-4367fc680d41" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="11a6d0a5-4add-4647-9c0c-7a2f724c255e">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="7b605698-6c4c-461a-9b1d-2d2d78f45275" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="4199b8a8-8f7e-4092-9758-793bda2b6232">The first line contains a single integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="1683abb8-f9f0-413a-a22a-ff3c371f874e" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="1653bfa8-e409-4c66-bb66-9d3c75f4c545"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="13b168f0-f160-4c1c-8c45-f6a4dab023ae"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D461 TEX-I" data-ref="54bbe7ad-7f08-4962-aa10-6a6b2b4e78c4"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="3607b761-4da1-48c1-a24f-e3f53e7d878a"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="9bf1f0f5-7d2b-473a-a675-a0a614b3b121"><mi data-ref="3f0eaaa8-288a-48cf-a102-c5ebe427242b">t</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, the minimum degree of the B-Tree.</li><li data-ref="192a1da5-85c9-44df-9716-7676a6d2b5bb">The second line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="a69d74fc-8007-4f54-840f-54be5f106b43" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="070f2b92-d58e-4ae2-98ef-384c550dcc15"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="90bd2340-23f3-417c-8fb5-e74ee5c32b36"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="0efa0c55-c597-49c6-841a-84da7f471582"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="cd5258d3-cad8-4072-9f3b-bafb9f2ad0b3"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="73cb964a-89b9-428f-ae18-acd214d12c1c"><mi data-ref="8822c702-e16e-42f6-b9b8-558b4ee4fc81">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the number of keys to be inserted.</li><li data-ref="05ef1e7f-5bd9-438c-9d34-a91faa44425d">The third line contains <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="28ae27b3-68bb-42d8-bf46-841654f6ca26" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="d54a26fe-d76f-44bb-ab65-1855e6899a97"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="da8a6dab-ebeb-4ce6-99fe-2231b1c70fdd"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="e22d6061-e174-4a2c-82ef-401cf59ac2c2"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="84e6de83-5f27-4118-b9f0-234cefc6e89e"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="e5eb2f15-ee44-4e7e-a22f-679626e228f6"><mi data-ref="5810fa1b-8d63-4801-a879-67f1ed5c79e2">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> space-separated integers â€” the keys to be inserted into the B-Tree.</li><li data-ref="06ce63e9-9ffd-48f9-8d42-ee693de9fcd1">The fourth line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="052322e4-7344-49fb-8217-1fa173b33bec" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="648738d6-d380-411a-8d53-ed5124a3e1ac"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="35573205-68c6-420e-b3a5-2a127a3901e2"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D451 TEX-I" data-ref="e676ec9d-3949-4fab-82df-5fe600c4e72b"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="1b9e31d6-10d8-432c-b041-8216faa51bc2"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="ee1873d6-5399-4385-825b-305066910432"><mi data-ref="6aaad025-f428-4313-86d7-b8a032781fab">d</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, the number of keys to delete.</li><li data-ref="a8875763-51c6-42dd-9db3-5ace7bb6250e">The fifth line contains <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML"