ayed"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="a4ec4e5c-9b8e-4a95-8914-87ab8df0ade4" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="bb574b4e-7f02-418b-99bc-22c88e8fa3fd"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="86cc42aa-4d14-4f26-ae55-6f5c8f1bbd5d"><p data-ref="771896ca-9802-4f64-88bb-9fdc9ef26aa7" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">You are given <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="26d4c6d5-4123-479f-886b-30906e981ebe" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="727655cf-a30a-475c-a69c-840b5cf7a61e"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="491fddbe-4062-4a46-acaa-5f502caa9a1d"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="72509006-4e66-4ecd-9ba4-99f9eef89fa0"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="15bd03a7-ddaa-4f5a-b43c-4a17b3742950"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="6fdeb02e-0369-48a3-a4e1-dd8c0ee328fb"><mi data-ref="f09da378-1201-4c0f-bf34-92993df9036f">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> items, each with a specific weight and value. You have a knapsack with a maximum capacity <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="ae3d329d-7135-4646-9220-125bba8645f7" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="9481bdca-9575-455d-a513-5c66c4639674"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="484d66d8-9683-45e4-b36a-8c648a99b8f6"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="8b61a842-fc61-47f4-ab3b-61914182b0ea"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="bddab9fc-7f38-4fa6-a4c7-9b36ac850eaa"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="195c2f0f-43b6-4301-a61d-18b55f942fc9"><mi data-ref="43416136-1c17-41a8-8a37-e419784a9409">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>. Your goal is to select a subset of these items such that the total weight is less than or equal to <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="48b4b4d5-0fc6-4140-872f-3322c6b8f1d1" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="df29521d-1f53-4250-90b6-d53f44772b2c"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="b5b8231b-f8e5-4eb7-96bd-8fbc14cea800"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="128cfb8d-79c2-4349-a15a-8b93026f16c2"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="032a0c9c-1983-4b67-84c8-400ebdfba28c"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="a5fb6714-382a-456e-b152-21529cf3d63e"><mi data-ref="0cdf6a71-93d5-44c7-8a4d-604236ac34eb">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, and the total value is as large as possible.</p><p data-ref="ea2a2285-6be3-4927-839b-106eeb27210f" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="27288006-5a97-4bc4-a0c5-429e4a9108a0"></p><p data-ref="7ad6346c-0628-4cd3-887a-7f7010b9f332" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">This is the classic 0/1 Knapsack problem, where each item can either be included once or excluded from the knapsack.</p><p data-ref="20f6e70c-4ac0-4281-9601-025374dd196c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="2b164268-fe9c-42c3-90c8-5ff29c725a5f"></p><p data-ref="14c11649-d8c9-43eb-b2bf-e97f5de1a0c1" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="f99d966e-d585-4a5c-a320-4163d4704d73">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="f1d006ac-1dd9-4614-9e40-be6ac284a7a3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="e53e1b29-d170-4ff2-982a-ea6efae2e412">The first line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="2abc7ef9-8000-4a3b-b89a-e70912c46c62" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="6a67260c-58f3-4a75-ad75-717d39686f0d"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="426b1e65-0384-4394-991f-9995139de441"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="1a5ef8f3-26bc-4785-8ef2-275fe61081d6"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="831bc1af-f576-4707-adc5-9ab82b8c2ea9"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="3c39c6b9-8d36-4471-a8a1-50df5a50b7bf"><mi data-ref="682588fa-f1cf-41ae-a795-ee23b04dd0dc">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the number of items to consider for the knapsack.</li><li data-ref="dc6d005d-fdba-4ba6-8a0f-cc2e2ab3b64b">The second line contains <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="b8e8cc89-39e5-40cc-8310-a5fc3226e5e4" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="f327d357-c546-4412-8772-3228bcb15bd6"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="03419da8-8893-4ccd-8a4c-604bf7bdde02"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="9f10c6d5-aa52-4256-b688-b884cd54562a"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="39803f79-9849-447a-a889-18ce9696ab0f"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="b2db4306-c036-40d4-842e-ccc9e668cd4e"><mi data-ref="54ae70c0-ed74-418b-9550-64ae936e72db">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> space-separated integers, representing the weights of the items.</li><li data-ref="05bc5c0f-ad6d-4902-8542-2d73feea0d20">The third line contains <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="71c5dcb8-5fe9-40c2-9bb2-685d3af7bb6e" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="51c62105-f975-4446-9378-8bf30ef41f79"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="dc6193aa-47ac-4d77-8253-d4055d1e4c71"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="b99e70db-d156-4acb-916e-a35e1a8ae7c2"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="d88e7a87-b438-495f-b436-1ce66e4ae4e8"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="6309a1c1-4edc-46a3-a8cf-8a5b652e278f"><mi data