lid black;" data-ref="0a9bc609-2e56-4e23-ad2c-368a1f34ab8d" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="78429fa8-e225-4e49-9946-455ebd44296d"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="90fd0d85-e2b6-48ae-aa13-f90f4cd989c2"><p data-ref="38e8ff58-ff5d-4355-83d4-caf9db29a6c3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to solve the 0/1 Knapsack Problem using backtracking approach. The program aims to maximize the total value of items that can be included in a knapsack without exceeding its capacity</p><p data-ref="dcccc6e2-972b-4998-a13b-fb7eb887104d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="373e4c69-72f2-47bb-9342-1df7aa6f206c"></p><p data-ref="1d324be6-fee3-437c-b8fb-0083a39ae907" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="ec1fe362-7007-4033-a14f-01a2445b5fde">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="4c419d4b-5c29-405b-a739-64be8dd00a3d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="4b211e36-b15f-48bc-bb2b-946b45d0c662">The first line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="7bbe2079-d07a-4958-9680-99126623755d" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="9d600904-34a4-467b-b8ed-8fa9a0b678c4"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="ffa70096-1a4d-4f35-b581-41341c0fda72"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="93aa39e3-53f7-45f7-927f-d301497e28b7"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="5072b289-8680-4fb4-b2b6-16aefd290e22"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="149b41f4-e187-4761-b47e-16a71dd42f05"><mi data-ref="ffe87f76-0438-4624-9f0e-c9adea408e62">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the number of items.</li><li data-ref="7a9c91ce-fa44-4455-82e7-fd7f0828599c">The next <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="9b5d31a9-dbf5-4fec-b240-4e48d536f12c" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="87952102-9f84-40ed-b4bd-73837755dbad"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="831e216b-dd1a-4104-8a7d-331fba80aa0f"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="30ecb49f-0512-40d9-9540-dbd10a99357c"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="71c6b0f8-9f09-45a6-9777-df3f0d885703"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="fc9f8c2c-41a9-463c-9fee-7f5d108417da"><mi data-ref="68fa6f80-1f32-4108-8df8-c27318ffff25">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> lines each contain two space-separated integers: the value and weight of an item.</li><li data-ref="3706ad1e-d4e8-4105-ac9a-0784e14